            "review_title": "Review at Mon Ngon Sai Thanh Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Sandra Tang\nHanoi, Vietnam7 contributions\n0\nPleasant Southern Style Food\nNov 2018 • Family\nI came to know about this place from my brother who lives in Hanoi for the past 5 years. He recommended me to go here for nice southern style food so I decided to give it a try with my husband and my mother in law.\n\nFirst impression - it was quite spacious, nicely decorated and clean place.\nSecond impression - the staff were like lost sheeps in chaos (honest opinion!)\n\nWhen we were trying to make some orders, most of the dishes that we would like to try were all out of stocks (reason that they gave - we do not have anymore!) - so my thoughts were like (you should have known that it is Saturday and expecting crowds).\n\nAnyway, we settled with some dishes and they were pretty decent. The food tasted good and pleasant to eat.\nRecommendation:\n- Banh Xeo : literally mean 'sizzling pancake' in English - quite good\n- Banh Khot : Mini pancake with shrimps - crispy on the outside with sliced pork belly, prawn and bean sprouts inside - quite good (you should try)\n- Crispy rice with fish sauce dip - it was ok (but totally instagram worthy!)\n- Stir fried glass noodles with crab - pretty decent\n- Sweet and sour prawn soup - it was good (I like this one)\n- Stewed fish - quite spicy and salty but not bad\n- Fresh spring rolls - not too bad\n- Steamed giant tiger-prawns in coconut - this is quite interesting (I would love the coconut taste to be stronger)\n- Sai Thanh baked chicken in salt crust - it was tender, juicy and pretty good.\n- Coconut smoothie - according to my mother in law, it was like the best smoothie she had in Hanoi (it was pretty good - you should try)\n\nPricing wise - I would say quite decent with the quantity of food, affordable and you do not feel like you are being charged overly for local food.\n\nOverall experience was quite good, beside the points where they do not have a lot of things on the menu and the staff were lost. I would say it is average. If you would like to have a quick fix on your southern food with a reasonable price, this is the place for you. (Note: please do not go on Sunday! It looked like a war zone with screaming and running children)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 26, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
